The Makefile of the repository evaluates this node, so the evaluation stands in for
running the go command by hand: the go command may switch to the toolchain
that go.mod asks for, as it does outside litar.
@<Go Project@/Filters@/go command settings@+
export GOTOOLCHAIN=auto
@

The commands are built in a view that adds the file set binaries to the go module;
the node maps bin of the repository into the view at the command directory of Go Project.
@<Litar Build@/commands@=
@<@|Go Project@/Filters@/build commands@+go module@+binaries@>
@

The source tree is every file of the composition, written into src of the repository,
which the node maps into the view as the file set source tree;
a file set added to the composition must be added to this view.
The input of the filter names the directory to write to.
@<Litar Build@/source files@=
@<Litar Build@/Internals@/source directory@|Litar Build@/Filters@/write files@+go module@+build@+tests@+source tree@>
@
@<Litar Build@/Internals@/source directory@=src@

Every file of the view outside the destination is written to a temporary name beside
its place in the destination and renamed there, so a failed write keeps the old file;
other files of the destination are left alone.
An executable file gets mode 755 and any other file 644.
The filter prints each written path, in sorted order.
@<Litar Build@/Filters@/write files@=#!/bin/sh
set -e
dest=$(cat)
find . -path "./$dest" -prune -o -type f -printf '%P\n' | LC_ALL=C sort |
while IFS= read -r f; do
	mkdir -p "$dest/$(dirname "$f")"
	cat "$f" > "$dest/$f.litar-new"
	if [ -x "$f" ]; then mode=755; else mode=644; fi
	chmod "$mode" "$dest/$f.litar-new"
	mv "$dest/$f.litar-new" "$dest/$f"
	echo "$f"
done
@

The Makefile installs the MCP server for Cursor by piping this script to python3
with the configuration file, the litar binary, and the directory of the grounds.
Only the litar entry is set, so other servers stay,
and the file is replaced at once, so an interrupted run keeps the old file.
@<Litar Build@/MCP configuration script@=
import json, os, sys
path, litar, grounds = sys.argv[1:]
try:
    with open(path) as f:
        text = f.read()
except FileNotFoundError:
    text = ''
config = json.loads(text) if text.strip() else {}
config.setdefault('mcpServers', {})['litar'] = {
    'command': litar, 'args': ['-a'], 'env': {'LITAR_LIBRARY': grounds}}
os.makedirs(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(path)), exist_ok=True)
with open(path + '.litar-new', 'w') as f:
    json.dump(config, f, indent=2)
    f.write('\n')
os.replace(path + '.litar-new', path)
@

@<Chunk@/Litar Build@=
{"description": "What the Makefile of the repository evaluates to build, sync, and install litar."}
@
@<Chunk@/Litar Build@/commands@=
{"description": "Build litar and litar-web into bin of the repository."}
@
@<Chunk@/Litar Build@/source files@=
{"description": "Write every file of the composition into src of the repository."}
@
@<Chunk@/Litar Build@/Internals@/source directory@=
{"description": "Directory of the view that receives the source tree."}
@
@<Chunk@/Litar Build@/Filters@/write files@=
{"description": "Write every file of the view into the directory named on stdin."}
@
@<Chunk@/Litar Build@/MCP configuration script@=
{"description": "Python script that sets the litar entry of a Cursor MCP configuration."}
@
